# CleanEgypt / Project Rules & Guidelines

## 1. Core Business Logic & Economy (STRICT)
- **TOKEN-ONLY SYSTEM:** The internal wallet and database `balance` represent TOKENS ONLY. 
- **NO FIAT IN WALLET:** Never use "EGP", "USD", or any other fiat currency symbols when displaying the user's internal balance.
- **STRIPE CHARGES:** Stripe strictly charges in USD (e.g., "$5 for 50 Tokens"). Do not calculate or display exchange rates.
- **USER ROLES:** - Clients: Buy Tokens to boost or post tasks.
  - Workers (Executors): Buy Subscriptions to unlock and view client phone numbers.

## 2. Backend (Supabase Edge Functions & Deno)
- **DENO ENVIRONMENT:** All Supabase Edge Functions must use Deno standards.
- **ESM IMPORTS ONLY:** Strictly use `https://esm.sh/` for external packages. DO NOT use `npm:` or Node.js style imports.
- **STRIPE HTTP CLIENT:** When initializing Stripe in Edge Functions, you MUST include: `httpClient: Stripe.createFetchHttpClient()`.
- **CORS IS MANDATORY:** Every function must handle `OPTIONS` requests and return headers: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` and `Access-Control-Allow-Methods: POST, OPTIONS`. (Crucial for mobile browsers).
- **ZERO-TRUST SECURITY:** Always verify the `Authorization` header. Fetch the user via Supabase Auth and verify their `user.id` matches the request before creating any Stripe Intents.
- **ERROR HANDLING:** Use `catch (error: any)` in Edge Functions to prevent TypeScript build errors.

## 3. Frontend (React / Vite / Tailwind)
- **MOBILE-FIRST UI:** Never hide critical action buttons (e.g., "Top Up", "Add Money", "Subscribe") on mobile devices using classes like `hidden sm:flex` or `hidden md:block`. Critical UI must be visible on all screen sizes.
- **STRIPE GUARDS:** Always verify that `VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` exists before attempting to render Stripe `<Elements />`. Log an error to the console if it is missing.
- **CLEAN CODE:** Avoid nested ternary operators in JSX. Keep components modular.